---
slug: signup
method: post
---
{%- comment -%}
  Role-aware signup.

  This exists instead of the module's POST /users because that page passes
  roles: null, so every account it creates falls back to USER_DEFAULT_ROLE. Our
  product requires the visitor to choose guest or host, so the choice has to
  reach commands/user/create.

  Everything below the role allow-list is the module's: validation, the user
  row, the profile, the surrounding transaction and the user_created event. We
  add a role and nothing else, which is why there is no override here.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  function current_profile = 'modules/user/helpers/current_profile'

  # platformos-check-disable DeprecatedTag, UnreachableCode
  include 'modules/user/helpers/can_do_or_redirect', requester: current_profile, do: 'signup.create', access_callback: null, entity: null, return_url: '/'
  # platformos-check-enable DeprecatedTag, UnreachableCode

  comment
    Never trust the submitted role. Anything that is not exactly 'host' is a
    guest, so a tampered field cannot mint an admin or an unknown role that
    would make every can_do check log a warning.
  endcomment
  assign role = context.params.role
  unless role == 'host'
    assign role = 'guest'
  endunless
  assign roles = []
  assign roles << role

  assign email = context.params.email | strip | downcase

  comment
    Verify before creating anything, and before the DB work. The command reads
    the token from context.params itself and resolves provider and secret from
    the CAPTCHA_DEFAULT_* constants, so no key appears here.

    It fails closed: a missing secret, an unknown provider or a transport error
    all land on valid: false. That is the right default, but it does mean an
    unset CAPTCHA_DEFAULT_SECRET blocks every signup rather than quietly
    letting them through, which is why the constants go in before this deploys.

    result.errors arrives already translated, so it goes straight to the form.
  endcomment
  function captcha = 'modules/captchas/commands/captcha/verify', provider: null, secret: null, token: null, response_field_name: null, remote_ip: null, expected_sitekey: null, expected_hostname: null, min_score: null, expected_action: null

  unless captcha.valid
    assign values = context.params
    assign values.password = ''
    assign values.role = role
    render 'signup/form', values: values, errors: captcha.errors
    break
  endunless

  function object = 'modules/user/commands/user/create', email: email, password: context.params.password, first_name: context.params.first_name, last_name: context.params.last_name, roles: roles, hook_params: context.params

  if object.valid
    function _ = 'modules/user/commands/session/create', validate_password: false, user_id: object.id, email: null, password: null, hook_params: null, skip_otp: null

    comment
      Both roles land on / for now. Once the pages exist a host belongs on
      /account/listings and a guest on /listings.
    endcomment
    redirect_to '/'
  else
    comment
      Re-render rather than redirect, so the field errors and what was typed
      survive. The password is dropped on purpose.
    endcomment
    assign values = context.params
    assign values.password = ''
    assign values.role = role
    render 'signup/form', values: values, errors: object.errors
  endif
-%}
